[
    {
        "content": "<p>Does Roc partially evaluate the parts of function bodies that work with comptime known parameters, or if there is at least one runtime param, the whole function becomes runtime-only?</p>",
        "id": 632819252,
        "sender_full_name": "notramo",
        "timestamp": 1792347558
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"roc\"><pre><span></span><code>add = |a, b| (a * 5) + b\n\nadd(1, getUserInput()?)\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is <code>(a * 5)</code> computed at comptime or runtime?</p>",
        "id": 632819590,
        "sender_full_name": "notramo",
        "timestamp": 1792347756
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>runtime, and it would still be comptime if add were curried...but you could get it to be comptime if you separated the arithmetic expressions like so: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">captured</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">captured</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 632822008,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard Feldman",
        "timestamp": 1792349293
    },
